  {
   "id": "s01",
   "text": "Salem, 1692. Witches *burned at the stake.*",
   "frames": 137
  },
  {
   "id": "s02",
   "text": "Except... *nobody was burned.*",
   "frames": 79
  },
  {
   "id": "s03",
   "text": "Salem: *the burning myth.*",
   "frames": 66
  },
  {
   "id": "s04",
   "text": "It started with two girls having strange *fits.*",
   "frames": 114
  },
  {
   "id": "s05",
   "text": "Soon, over *200* people were accused.",
   "frames": 102
  },
  {
   "id": "s06",
   "text": "Courts accepted *spectral evidence.* Basically, dreams.",
   "frames": 141
  },
  {
   "id": "s07",
   "text": "*19* people were executed.",
   "frames": 94
  },
  {
   "id": "s08",
   "text": "By *hanging.* Not fire.",
   "frames": 76
  },
  {
   "id": "s09",
   "text": "In English law, witchcraft was a *felony.*",
   "frames": 107
  },
  {
   "id": "s10",
   "text": "And felons were *hanged.*",
   "frames": 75
  },
  {
   "id": "s11",
   "text": "Burning was more of a *European* thing.",
   "frames": 106
  },
  {
   "id": "s12",
   "text": "One man, Giles Corey, *refused to plead.*",
   "frames": 113
  },
  {
   "id": "s13",
   "text": "Others died in *jail.*",
   "frames": 78
  },
  {
   "id": "s14",
   "text": "By *1693,* it was over.",
   "frames": 100
  },
  {
   "id": "s15",
   "text": "Later, jurors *apologised.*",
   "frames": 93
  },
  {
   "id": "s16",
   "text": "In *2022,* the last accused was finally cleared.",
   "frames": 145
  },
  {
   "id": "s17",
   "text": "So where did the fire *come from?*",
   "frames": 80
  },
  {
   "id": "s18",
   "text": "Movies and European witch trials, *mixed together.*",
   "frames": 123
  },
  {
   "id": "s19",
   "text": "Witches burned at Salem: *zero.*",
   "frames": 94
  },
  {
